# Build-context exclusions for the metaserve image (see Dockerfile).
#
# The image is code + site only - it bakes NO data - so the catalogue must not
# ride into the build context either. Without this, `COPY . .` in the build
# stage ships the whole data/ tree into the builder layer, which would make the
# image build time and cache invalidation grow with the catalogue: exactly what
# dropping the baked artifact was meant to stop. Nothing in metaserve's build
# path reads data/ (the only embedded files are schema/*.json and
# internal/importer/audiblegenres.json).
data/

# Git history is not read by any build step (added_at lives in the records now,
# so no stage walks the log) and it is the largest thing in the repo.
.git
.github

# Rebuilt inside the site stage by `yarn install` / `yarn build`; copying the
# host's copies in would defeat the dependency layer and can mix architectures.
site/node_modules
site/dist
site/.astro

# Local runtime/build leftovers that must never end up in an image.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite.gz
bin/
cache/
